From 655af8f61b646508b0ff19606a1969118763626c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:59:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] git_ui: Say when each review note was written

A thread showed who wrote each note but not when, so an old remark and
one from a minute ago read the same. The note's time from GitLab now
sits beside its author: on a thread folded to a chip, on the opening
comment, on each reply, and on the threads on the merge request itself.
It reads "Today at" or "Yesterday at" and the time, else the date and
the time, in the reader's own time zone and format. A comment not yet
posted has no time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
